>> C1: Copy here the declaration of each new or changed `struct' or
>> `struct' member, global or static variable, `typedef', or
>> enumeration.  Identify the purpose of each in 25 words or less.

static struct list mlfq_list[PRI_MAX + 1]; 
static fixedpoint_t load_avg;
int nice;                          
fixedpoint_t recent_cpu;
typedef int32_t fixedpoint_t;  

mlfq_list holds per-priority queues for the multilevel feedback queue schedule - this allows efficient scheduling at each priority level.
load_avg tracks the average number of ready threads over time for load balancing in the MLFS.
nice indicates how “nice” a thread is (how willing it can be to yield CPU time) for MLFQS priority calculations.
recent_cpu stores a thread’s recent CPU usage in fixed-point format, used to compute dynamic priority under MLFQS.
fixedpoint_t is a new data_type that defines a 32-bit fixed-point type for fractional arithmetic needed by MLFQS load and CPU calculations.
